# oralsurgeryassess.com — environment variables (AI Notes, and the gated implant preview)
#
# Scope every one of these to PRODUCTION ONLY in the Vercel dashboard, or
# password-protect preview deployments. A preview URL otherwise runs the same
# code against the same keys, on a hostname nobody is watching.
#
# The repo is PUBLIC. Never commit a real .env or paste a key into any file in
# it: keys live only in the Vercel dashboard.

# --- Auth: staff accounts (the normal way in) ------------------------------
# Sign-in is email + password (no second factor, by the owner's decision, so
# each person's password should be long and used nowhere else). The
# accounts live in a Vercel Global Config store (formerly Edge Config), one
# item per person, and the owner manages them at /ai-notes/admin/ without
# redeploying. The store holds sign-in details only: nothing about any patient.
#
# Connection string for the store. Vercel adds it for you when the store is
# connected to this project (Storage -> the store -> Projects -> Connect), as
# GLOBAL_CONFIG, or EDGE_CONFIG on an older store; either name works. It
# looks like  https://global-config.vercel.com/<storeId>?token=<readToken>
# UNSET: accounts are off and sign-in is by APP_USERS passcodes exactly as
# before. SET BUT MALFORMED: accounts are unavailable AND passcodes are not
# reopened because of it; the function log says which.
GLOBAL_CONFIG=

# A Vercel access token, used ONLY to write to the store (adding staff, new
# setup links, disabling, finishing a setup). Read by api/users.mjs and
# api/account.mjs through api/_accounts.mjs and nowhere else. Vercel's tokens
# are scoped to a team with full access: this token can change projects and
# deployments, not just the store. Treat it like the AWS secret: Production
# scope only, never in a file. Create it at vercel.com -> Account Settings ->
# Tokens, scoped to this team, with an expiry you will notice.
VERCEL_API_TOKEN=

# Only if the project belongs to a team rather than a personal (Hobby) account:
# the team id (team_...), from Team Settings -> General. Leave unset otherwise.
# VERCEL_TEAM_ID=

# THE ALLOWANCES ARE SMALL, and on Hobby going over one BLOCKS THE STORE FOR
# 30 DAYS (nobody could sign in). Vercel's Hobby page, September 2026: 100
# writes and 100,000 reads a month; store size given as 1 MB (8 KB on older
# pages). So: sign-in never writes; only admin actions and finishing a setup
# do (one each); api/users.mjs allows 5 an hour and 10 a day per instance and
# refuses to add anyone once the store would pass 7 KB (about twenty staff);
# and nothing an outsider can send forces a store read (see api/_store.mjs).
# Check the Usage tab now and then.

# ROTATING SESSION_SECRET (below) signs everyone out, as it always has.
# Passwords are unaffected: everyone just signs in again.

# --- Auth: passcodes (transition only) ------------------------------------
# While accounts are being set up, the old passcodes keep working so the
# owner cannot be locked out. With a store configured they work ONLY while
# APP_USERS is set; delete APP_USERS (and redeploy) once everyone has an
# account, and passcode sign-in and passcode-era sessions stop at once.
#
# One passcode per clinician: initials, a colon, the passcode; commas between.
# The initials are who is signed in, and appear beside Lock. Each passcode a
# passphrase of at least six characters, not four digits: the throttle in
# api/auth.mjs is per warm instance and will not stop a determined guesser.
# A passcode or set of initials listed twice is refused for both entries.
# Removing someone is deleting their pair and redeploying.
# e.g. APP_USERS=AM:<passphrase>,SM:<passphrase>
APP_USERS=

# Transition only: who may open /ai-notes/admin/ while APP_USERS is set, by
# initials, before any admin account exists. This is how the owner creates the
# first account (his own, as an admin). Ignored once APP_USERS is removed;
# from then on an admin is an account with the admin role. UNSET MEANS NOBODY.
# e.g. ADMIN_USERS=AM
ADMIN_USERS=

# Who may open the implant tool, on top of being signed in. Initials (of an
# account, or from APP_USERS), commas between; case and spacing do not matter. The tool is a
# preview whose clinical figures are drafts, so it is kept to its author until
# they are reviewed. UNSET MEANS CLOSED TO EVERYONE, including him: an unset
# variable must never be what opens a door. Add a colleague by adding their
# initials here and redeploying; no new password is involved.
# e.g. IMPLANT_USERS=AM
IMPLANT_USERS=

# APP_PASSCODE, the old single shared code, is NO LONGER HONOURED (removed
# 19 September 2026). Anyone using it was signed in as nobody. If it is set,
# api/auth.mjs ignores it and says so in the function log. Do not set it.

# Signs the session cookie. Not in the original manifest — added because a
# bare boolean cookie can be forged by anyone who can type document.cookie.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Transcription ------------------------------------------------------
SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=

# Processing region. Speechmatics decide the region by the hostname called and
# nothing else; the DPIA (§2.7) records EU1. The default is EU1, and
# api/transcribe.mjs refuses to start against any host that is not
# eu1./eu2.asr.api.speechmatics.com. Leave unset, or set exactly this:
# SPEECHMATICS_API_BASE=https://eu1.asr.api.speechmatics.com/v2

# --- Extraction ---------------------------------------------------------
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=eu-west-2

# Declares the data residency the DPIA claims, and is ENFORCED at runtime:
# api/extract.mjs refuses to sign a request whose model id or region contradicts
# it. "eu" or "uk".
#
# UK-ONLY IS NOT CURRENTLY ACHIEVABLE HERE. Bedrock does not offer single-region
# routing for Claude in eu-west-2 — London is a Global/EU region, not an
# "in-region only" one — and every current Claude model requires an inference
# profile prefix; a bare model id returns HTTP 400. Setting this to "uk" will
# therefore refuse every working configuration, deliberately, rather than let the
# footprint quietly widen. If UK-only is a hard requirement, the extraction step
# needs a different provider.
DATA_RESIDENCY=eu

# Must carry the "eu." prefix while DATA_RESIDENCY=eu. A "global." or "us."
# profile would place patient audio outside the adequacy area and is refused
# before the request is signed.
#
# NOTE ON THE FORMAT: the Claude 5 generation has no version suffix. Earlier
# models looked like anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0; Opus 5, Sonnet 5
# and Fable 5 are simply anthropic.claude-opus-5 and so on, because they carry no
# ARN-versioned model IDs. A trailing -v1:0 on one of these is wrong and will
# fail. They remain reachable through InvokeModel on bedrock-runtime, which is
# the endpoint api/extract.mjs uses.
BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0

# SUFFIX RULE - this bites both ways, so read it before changing the model.
#   Claude 5 generation (Opus 5, Sonnet 5): NO version suffix.
#       eu.anthropic.claude-opus-5
#   Anything earlier (Sonnet 4.5, Haiku 4.5): FULL dated suffix, required.
#       eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
# Getting it wrong gives "The provided model identifier is invalid", which reads
# like a typo rather than a generational naming change.
#
# To find the exact string: Bedrock console -> Model catalog -> the model. The id
# is in the page URL and in the Details table.
#
# ACCOUNT GATING, Aug 2026: eu.anthropic.claude-opus-5 and .claude-sonnet-5 were
# both refused with "not available for this account" and a pointer to AWS Sales.
# Verified in the console playground with administrator credentials, so it is not
# IAM, not signing, not the eu. prefix. Sonnet 4.5 works on the same account via
# the same EU profile. The Claude 5 generation appears to be withheld from new
# accounts pending billing history. See AWS-ACCESS.md if you want to pursue it.

# Worth testing rather than assuming. This task is structuring a transcript at
# temperature 0, and the failure mode that matters is the model being helpful and
# inventing risks nobody named. Swap this to eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5,
# redeploy, and re-run the seven fixtures in tests/. If Sonnet passes
# extraction-vague and patient-raises-risk as cleanly, it is the right choice and
# a great deal cheaper per consultation.
